one re-ask inserts its note on its own line before the final line.
Jinja whitespace control is reproduced with {{- and -}}.

Intentional deviation (spec P7 §5.2, X-13): upstream has no existing-
discussion block. When the pipeline supplies one (.discussion, already
rendered: the fixed header and the threads inside an adaptive code fence),
it follows the description and precedes the diff; without one nothing is
rendered, so the prompt is byte-identical to the one without the feature.

Intentional deviation (v1.1 spec WP-11e2, X-19): upstream reviews a pull
request in one call. When the pipeline reviews a large one in several parts,
each part's prompt gets one line (.part_header, the fixed sentence of
PartHeader) right before the diff, telling the model which part it sees.
With one part nothing is rendered, so the prompt is byte-identical to the
one without the feature.

Intentional deviation (v1.1 spec WP-11c, X-22, RC-8): upstream has no
repository context. When context.repo.enabled is set and the pipeline found
uses of the changed symbols outside the pull request, it supplies one block
(.repo_context, already rendered: the fixed sentence of repoctx.Header and
the entries "[path:line] uses symbol" with their snippets inside an
adaptive code fence). It follows the discussion block and precedes the part
line and the diff; without one nothing is rendered, so the prompt is
byte-identical to the one without the feature. In a review in several parts
an entry whose file is itself changed by the pull request, in a file another
part reviews (or that no part reviews), ends its first line with a mark in
parentheses: "(changed in this pull request; reviewed in part J)" or
"(changed in this pull request; not reviewed)". The uses are read from the
head commit, so they show the new version of that file.
